  "summary": "simple-probe-utils postinstall exfiltrates host identity to Burp Collaborator endpoint",
  "details": "The package advertises itself as a lightweight string formatting helper, but ships a postinstall.js that runs on `npm install`. postinstall.js line 13 invokes child_process.exec on a curl command (line 11) that reads the installer's hostname and username via $(hostname) and $(whoami) and sends them as query parameters to a hardcoded Burp Collaborator subdomain (pzs5w7ntzhsnepwk564lyfdci3oucl0a.oastify.com) over plain HTTP. The exported library code only implements trivial capitalize/truncate helpers unrelated to network I/O or host reconnaissance, so the install-time beacon is not incidental to the package's advertised functionality.",
